---
description: >-
  `swimlane.automaticLaneOrdering: true`: five lanes written so that the
  busy ones (Intake, Review, Delivery) are kept apart by two that only talk
  to each other (Archive, Records). The weighted-linear-arrangement pass
  moves the busy lanes next to each other, so the cross-lane edges get
  shorter; with the default (`false`) the lanes keep their source order.
config:
  swimlane:
    automaticLaneOrdering: true
---
swimlane-beta LR
  subgraph Intake
    A[Receive] --> B[Triage]
  end
  subgraph Archive
    X[Store]
  end
  subgraph Review
    C[Assess] --> D[Decide]
    D --> R[Reopen]
  end
  subgraph Records
    Y[Index]
  end
  subgraph Delivery
    E[Build] --> F[Ship]
  end
  B --> C
  D --> E
  B --> E
  R --> A
  X --> Y
  F --> X
